Package: Ribosome
Type: Package
Title: Steady-State Polysome Distributions of Capped and Decapped mRNA
Version: 0.1.0
Author: Nate Pollesch, Ricardo Urquidi Camacho, Ben Ernest, Michael Gilchrist
Maintainer: Ricardo Urquidi Camacho <rurquidi@vols.utk.edu>
Description: Computes the steady-state distribution of mRNA across polysome
    classes (number of bound ribosomes, 0 to imax) for a model in which
    transcripts are produced capped at rate lambda, gain ribosomes by
    initiation (kappa) and lose them by elongation and termination (tau), are
    decapped at rate mu, and are degraded from the ribosome-free decapped
    class at rate delta. Initiation and termination can depend on ribosome
    density. Includes summary statistics (class probabilities, mean, standard
    deviation and mode of ribosome load). Supports the manuscript figures in
    'Text/Paper final figures.Rmd' of the source repository.
License: What license is it under?
Encoding: UTF-8
